    "name": "Tupay — Ledger & Settlement Engine",
    "description": "Verification collection for the Tupay assessment.\n\n## Before you start\n\n```bash\nphp artisan migrate:fresh --seed\nphp artisan serve\n```\n\n## What is automated\n\nTwo things normally make an API collection painful here, and both are handled by pre-request scripts so you never have to paste a value by hand:\n\n1. **TOTP codes** rotate every 30 seconds. `POST /2fa/challenge` computes a valid RFC-6238 code from the seeded base32 secret at request time.\n2. **Webhook signatures** are HMAC-SHA256 over `{timestamp}.{raw body}`. The webhook requests build the raw body, sign it, and set both headers themselves.\n\nBearer tokens, elevated action tokens, and wallet ids are captured into collection variables by test scripts, so requests can simply be run in order.\n\n## Suggested order\n\nRun the folders top to bottom. `Happy path` must run before `Attacks` and `Ledger`, because it populates the token and wallet variables.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    { "key": "baseUrl", "value": "http://127.0.0.1:8000", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "email", "value": "trader@tupay.test", "type": "string" },
